<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8" standalone="yes"?><ns2:section xmlns:ns2="http://rest.cis.illinois.edu" id="53252" href="schedule/2015/fall/DANC/310/53252.xml"><parents><calendarYear id="2015" href="schedule/2015.xml">2015</calendarYear><term id="120158" href="schedule/2015/fall.xml">Fall 2015</term><subject id="DANC" href="schedule/2015/fall/DANC.xml">Dance</subject><course id="310" href="schedule/2015/fall/DANC/310.xml">World Dance Forms</course></parents><sectionNumber>AF2</sectionNumber><sectionTitle>African Dance</sectionTitle><creditHours>1 hours</creditHours><statusCode>A</statusCode><sectionText>Umfundalai is a contemporary African dance technique that comprises its movement vocabulary from dance traditions from the continent of Africa as well as societies throughout the Diaspora.  Contemporary African Dance uses Umfundalai to provide students with a rigorous movement experience that will focus on alignment, rhythm, and style as competencies in proficient, African-informed movement practice.</sectionText><partOfTerm>1</partOfTerm><sectionStatusCode>A</sectionStatusCode><enrollmentStatus>UNKNOWN</enrollmentStatus><startDate>2015-08-24Z</startDate><endDate>2015-12-09Z</endDate><meetings><meeting id="0"><type code="LAB">Laboratory</type><start>05:00 PM</start><end>06:20 PM</end><daysOfTheWeek>MW     </daysOfTheWeek><roomNumber>2500</roomNumber><buildingName>Krannert Center for Perf Arts</buildingName><instructors><instructor lastName="Ndiaye" firstName="M">Ndiaye, M</instructor></instructors></meeting></meetings></ns2:section>